  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Supporting Youths involvement on 2015 electoral process in Burundi</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This project seeks to increase knowledge on electoral issues and promote consideration for Human Rights by youths, and to increase communities&#x2019; awareness on election violence reduction in Burundi as well as protection for human rights defenders. 

The project aims to also contribute to improving peaceful cohabitation within Burundi&#x2019;s youths, when running electoral processes, through teaching responsible citizenship and good electoral practices, sensitisation and advocacy for respect of Human Rights. 

Experiences to be gained in this project on youth peaceful involvement in electoral processes will be shared with youths from DRC and Rwanda to enhance relations. Experiences from the project will also be exchanged with Burundian civil society organisations who need to be involved as relevant actors.</narrative>
  </description>
